## What the trip actually consists of

Strip away the photography and a Dubai desert safari is four things in a fixed order.

**The drive.** Around an hour each way from most Dubai hotels to the Lahbab dune field, which sits southeast of the city on the Dubai-Hatta road. Our base is at Al Awir on the edge of it. This part is not glamorous and it is a real share of the day.

**The dune bashing.** Twenty minutes or so of a trained driver taking a Land Cruiser up, along and down sand faces with the tyres let down. It is the part everyone films and the part that is shortest.

**The sunset stop.** Ten minutes on a ridge. In the hour before sunset the sand at Lahbab reads genuinely orange to red, which is where the photographs people remember come from.

**The camp.** Two to three hours. A camel ride, sandboarding, Arabic coffee and dates, a halal BBQ buffet, then belly dance, tanoura and fire shows.

That is it. Nobody is hiding a fifth thing, and the operators charging three times as much are selling a better camp and a newer car rather than a different desert.

The word safari does a lot of work here and it misleads people who arrive expecting wildlife. There are no animals in the dune field beyond the camels waiting at the camp. What the trip is actually about is the landscape and the evening, which is worth knowing before you book it for somebody who was picturing a game drive.

## Shared or private, which is the only real decision

Everything else is a variation on the four items above. This one changes the day.

A **shared** safari puts you in a Land Cruiser with five or six other guests and charges **per person**, from AED 99. A **private** safari gives you the vehicle and the pace and charges **per vehicle**, from AED 650.

| Group | Shared, per person | Private, per vehicle |
|---|---|---|
| 2 people | AED 198 | AED 650 |
| 4 people | AED 396 | AED 650 |
| 6 people | AED 594 | AED 650 |

Two people should share. Six people are AED 56 away from having the car to themselves, setting their own pace and being able to ask the driver to stop. [The full price list](/desert-safari-dubai/price/) has every package with its price basis on the row.

## How the booking works, start to finish

1. **Message us** with the date, the number of people and the ages if children are coming.
2. **We reply** with availability, the package we would put you on and the total in AED.
3. **You confirm.** Nothing is paid. There is no deposit on a standard booking.
4. **The day before**, we confirm the pickup window and take your hotel name or a map pin.
5. **On the day**, the driver arrives inside that window and you settle up during the trip.

We are reachable from 7am to 11pm, seven days a week. WhatsApp is the fastest route and it is answered by the people who run the base rather than a call centre.

The one thing worth saying at step one is anything that changes the drive: someone who gets carsick, is pregnant, has a bad back, or simply does not want the aggressive version. Our drivers adjust when they know in advance, and it is much harder to arrange in a shared car where the other five booked for the opposite.

## Which package suits which trip

The [evening safari](/desert-safari-dubai/evening-desert-safari/) is the default and the one most visitors mean. Camp, dinner, show.

The [morning safari](/desert-safari-dubai/morning-desert-safari/) is four to five hours, runs in cooler sand and puts you in an empty dune field. No camp dinner, no show. From June to September it is the only comfortable option, and with young children it is the better booking in any month.

The [overnight safari](/desert-safari-dubai/overnight-desert-safari/) adds a night at camp and sunrise over the dunes, at AED 250 per person.

If someone in the group would rather drive than be driven, the [safari with a quad session](/desert-safari-dubai/quad-bike-desert-safari/) at AED 199 per person builds a ride into the evening.

## Pickup, payment and getting out of it

**Hotel pickup and drop-off inside Dubai is free on every safari booking.** Transfers from Sharjah, Ajman, Abu Dhabi and Ras Al Khaimah are quoted with the booking, so you see the total before paying anything.

Payment is cash, card or bank transfer, settled on the day rather than upfront. Cancel more than 24 hours before and there is nothing to reclaim because nothing was paid. Inside 24 hours we will try to move you to another date rather than charge you.

We have run our base at Al Awir since 2020 and taken more than 17,000 guests into that dune field. The bookings that go well are almost always the ones where somebody said the group size and the ages in the first message.
